## Example

The following example evaluates \f$\log \Gamma(x)\f$, \f$\psi(x)\f$, and \f$\psi^{(2)}(x)\f$ inside a `Kokkos::parallel_for` kernel:

\code{.cpp}
#include <laplace/math/special.hpp>
#include <Kokkos_Core.hpp>

void compute_gamma_functions(const Kokkos::View<const double*>& x,
                             Kokkos::View<double*>& lg,
                             Kokkos::View<double*>& psi,
                             Kokkos::View<double*>& pg2,
                             int n) {
  Kokkos::parallel_for("eval_gamma", n, KOKKOS_LAMBDA(const int i) {
    const double x_val = x(i);
    lg(i)  = laplace::math::lgamma(x_val);
    psi(i) = laplace::math::digamma(x_val);
    pg2(i) = laplace::math::polygamma(2, x_val);
  });
}
\endcode

## Module functions

Functions in this module are called as `laplace::math::NAME`.

- \ref laplace::math::lgamma "lgamma()" — \f$\log \Gamma(x)\f$ via Boost.Math
- \ref laplace::math::digamma "digamma()" — \f$\psi(x)\f$ via Boost.Math
- \ref laplace::math::trigamma "trigamma()" — \f$\psi'(x)\f$ via Boost.Math
- \ref laplace::math::polygamma "polygamma()" — \f$\psi^{(n)}(x)\f$, \f$n \in \{0, \dots, 6\}\f$ (dispatches to `digamma()` for \f$n = 0\f$, `trigamma()` for \f$n = 1\f$, `own::polygamma()` for \f$n \ge 2\f$)
- \ref laplace::math::own::polygamma "own::polygamma()" — \f$\psi^{(n)}(x)\f$, \f$n \in \{0, \dots, 6\}\f$ via recurrence and asymptotic expansion
- \ref laplace::math::own::digamma "own::digamma()" — \f$\psi(x)\f$ via `own::polygamma(0, x)`
- \ref laplace::math::own::trigamma "own::trigamma()" — \f$\psi'(x)\f$ via `own::polygamma(1, x)`
*/
